Modes: Orchestrator

Purpose:
  Defines orchestrator modes and decision thresholds.

AgentModes:
  AUTO:
    Description: AI decides low-risk items
    Use: Standard development
  SUPERVISED:
    Description: AI recommends, human approves major decisions
    Use: Risky projects
  STRICT:
    Description: Human approval required for architecture, security, DB migration, release
    Use: Financial/security-critical
  AUDIT:
    Description: Analysis only, no modifications
    Use: Project analysis
  READ_ONLY:
    Description: Project analysis, no code changes
    Use: "Analyze project"

DecisionThreshold:
  LOW_RISK:
    Action: AI decides
    Examples: Code style, variable naming, small refactors
  MEDIUM_RISK:
    Action: AI recommends
    Examples: Library selection, configuration changes
  HIGH_RISK:
    Action: Human approval
    Examples: Architecture change, DB migration, security policy
  CRITICAL:
    Action: Human mandatory
    Examples: Production deployment, credential rotation, data deletion

HumanDecisionBoundary:
  AI decides:
    - Code implementation
    - Test creation
    - Documentation
    - Configuration (non-security)
  Human approves:
    - Architecture changes
    - Database migration
    - Security policy
    - Production destructive operations

OverengineeringGuard:
  AI MUST ask "Necessary?" for every recommendation.
  10k users → Kubernetes + Kafka is overengineering.

ComplexityBudget:
  LOW:
    Modular Monolith
  MEDIUM:
    Modular Monolith + async workers
  HIGH:
    Selective services
  CRITICAL:
    Distributed architecture

ModeRules:
  [MD1]  Default mode is AUTO for standard projects.
  [MD2]  STRICT mode requires human approval for critical decisions.
  [MD3]  READ_ONLY mode never modifies source code.
  [MD4]  Complexity budget MUST be respected.
  [MD5]  System can degrade to REDUCED, MINIMAL, or READ_ONLY.
  [MD6]  Degradation is automatic based on health checks.
  [MD7]  Recovery is automatic when conditions improve.
  [MD8]  Human is notified of mode changes.

DegradationModes:
  FULL:
    Description: All features operational
    Trigger: All components healthy
    Capabilities:
      - Full chain execution
      - All skills available
      - Full context loading
      - Human gates active

  REDUCED:
    Description: Non-critical features disabled
    Trigger: Minor component failure, resource pressure
    Capabilities:
      - Chain execution (skip optional stages)
      - Core skills only
      - Reduced context (lazy loading)
      - Human gates active for critical items
    Restrictions:
      - Skip observability stages
      - Skip optional testing stages
      - Use cached contexts only

  MINIMAL:
    Description: Essential features only
    Trigger: Major component failure, resource exhaustion
    Capabilities:
      - Basic chain execution (P1->D1->S1->C1 only)
      - Essential skills only
      - Minimal context
      - Human approval for all gates
    Restrictions:
      - No R1 (review) - human reviews manually
      - No DEP1 (deploy) - human deploys manually
      - No parallel execution
      - No caching

  READ_ONLY:
    Description: Analysis only, no modifications
    Trigger: System instability, audit mode
    Capabilities:
      - Read .sdd/ files
      - Analyze project structure
      - Generate reports
    Restrictions:
      - No file creation
      - No modifications
      - No chain execution
      - No state changes

DegradationTriggers:
  ResourceBased:
    Memory > 90%: REDUCED
    Memory > 95%: MINIMAL
    Disk < 1GB: READ_ONLY
    Token budget < 10%: MINIMAL

  ComponentBased:
    Skill registry unavailable: REDUCED
    Context cache corrupted: REDUCED
    Graph engine failed: MINIMAL
    State tracker failed: READ_ONLY

  FailureBased:
    1-2 stage failures: REDUCED
    3+ stage failures: MINIMAL
    Critical component failure: READ_ONLY

CircuitBreaker:
  failure_threshold: 3
  recovery_timeout: 60s
  success_threshold: 2
  half_open_max_requests: 5

State: +
  